      "normalized_sha256": "146fed052167b079e1650450e1ce639924212da85a65b3aba6d9be3d6e53c7e3",
      "rationale": "This is the exponent-zero base equation of the simplePower mathematical summary and directly defines its value when X is 1.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-146fed052167b079e1650450e1ce639924212da85a65b3aba6d9be3d6e53c7e3",
      "start_line": 13,
      "text": "  rule simplePower(1, _N) => true"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 16,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "60585bbb6d312b6f4f8499ebbf464f74ddf2e2181ec92b0e8af660b2838bc868",
      "rationale": "This guarded equation defines the simplePower summary for base 0 outside the already-covered X = 1 case.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-60585bbb6d312b6f4f8499ebbf464f74ddf2e2181ec92b0e8af660b2838bc868",
      "start_line": 15,
      "text": "  rule simplePower(X, 0) => X ==Int 0\n    requires X =/=Int 1"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 19,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "896a8a4fcf1778edbc32f433cc5724feec0edb677d9dea32a3e484bb2aecf746",
      "rationale": "This guarded equation defines the simplePower summary for base 1 outside the exponent-zero case.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-896a8a4fcf1778edbc32f433cc5724feec0edb677d9dea32a3e484bb2aecf746",
      "start_line": 18,
      "text": "  rule simplePower(X, 1) => false\n    requires X =/=Int 1"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 22,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "3ecd89403379532a7e0ba4d1d0747278594ded6e9d59f9925bdee477f6b5ddc3",
      "rationale": "This guarded equation defines the simplePower summary for the degenerate base -1 outside the exponent-zero case.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-3ecd89403379532a7e0ba4d1d0747278594ded6e9d59f9925bdee477f6b5ddc3",
      "start_line": 21,
      "text": "  rule simplePower(X, -1) => X ==Int -1\n    requires X =/=Int 1"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 25,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "e5a3d5202919810bbe675a2a77fceecdb470e4b5c07f803b5b3ecbed8f59041b",
      "rationale": "This equation is a base case in the mathematical summary, defining zero as not a power when the base magnitude is at least two.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-e5a3d5202919810bbe675a2a77fceecdb470e4b5c07f803b5b3ecbed8f59041b",
      "start_line": 24,
      "text": "  rule simplePower(0, N) => false\n    requires N <=Int -2 orBool N >=Int 2"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 31,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "d19d1bda5d0346f529812d8ff45415af253ed73e3bc020870bf8b1750eb773b9",
      "rationale": "This is the primary exact-factor recurrence defining simplePower by removing one factor on the guarded divisible case.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-d19d1bda5d0346f529812d8ff45415af253ed73e3bc020870bf8b1750eb773b9",
      "start_line": 27,
      "text": "  rule simplePower(X, N)\n    => simplePower((X -Int pyMod(X, N)) /Int N, N)\n    requires X =/=Int 0 andBool X =/=Int 1\n     andBool (N <=Int -2 orBool N >=Int 2)\n     andBool pyMod(X, N) ==Int 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 36,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "775415705833fb882b7bb2633fea60ea3123195b617f4a19ad0450c43e3dd4ae",
      "rationale": "This terminal equation completes the simplePower definition on the guarded nondivisible case.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-775415705833fb882b7bb2633fea60ea3123195b617f4a19ad0450c43e3dd4ae",
      "start_line": 33,
      "text": "  rule simplePower(X, N) => false\n    requires X =/=Int 0 andBool X =/=Int 1\n     andBool (N <=Int -2 orBool N >=Int 2)\n     andBool pyMod(X, N) =/=Int 0"
    }
  ],
